610 - Stand Like the Brave
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 610
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[G]O Christian, awake! 'tis the Master's [D]command;
[G]With [D]helmet and [Bm]shield, and a [D/A]sword [Am]in thy [D]hand,
[G]To [C]meet the [G/B]bold tempter, go, fearlessly [C]go,
[G]Then stand [Em]like the [D]brave, with [D7]thy [G]face [D]to [Bm]the foe.

Refrain:
[G]Stand like the brave, stand like the brave,
[G]Stand like the [C]brave, with thy [G/D]face to [D7]the [G]foe.

Verse 2:
[G]The cause of thy Master with vigor [D]defend;
[G]Be [D]watchful, be [Bm]zealous, and [D/A]fight [Am]to the [D]end;
[G]Wherever He leads thee, go, valiantly [C]go,
[G]Then stand [Em]like the [D]brave, with [D7]thy [G]face [D]to [Bm]the foe.

Verse 3:
[G]Press on, never doubting, thy Captain [D]is [G]near,
[G]With [D]grace to supply, [Bm]and with [D/A]comfort [Am]to [D]cheer;
[G]His [C]love, like [G/B]a stream in the desert [C]will flow;
[G]Then stand [Em]like the [D]brave, with [D7]thy [G]face [D]to [Bm]the foe.
